 "equipment_type": "Multi-load power meter",
 "applies_to": "Setra Power Meter (SPM) multi-load electrical meters; this entry covers each virtual load device (one per configured load).",
 "summary": "Each load on a Setra Power Meter appears as its own BACnet load device, with objects reserved for up to three CTs. The load device reports voltages, frequency, total real, reactive and apparent power, current, power factor, demand and energy totals, plus a block of per-CT readings. Energy totals are also offered as Large Analog Values.",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The meter shows up as more than one BACnet device: a root device for the voltage inputs and load device(s) with the object list below. The root and load lists are separate entries in this library.",
  "The list has no read/write column; all objects are shown read-only here (access inferred).",
  "Only the CT 1 block (AI 30-52, BV 1) is printed. The manual reserves AI 60-82 for CT 2 and AI 90-112 for CT 3 (CT 1 instance + 30 per CT), and BV 2/BV 3 for their polarity correction.",
  "Several unit cells look wrong in the PDF: AI 52 prints degrees-phase, AI 141/142 and LAV 2/3 swap kVAh and kvarh, and AI 43/44 and AI 145/146 print kvarh for kVAh totals. Units are kept as printed. AI 50 (phase angle) prints kvarh and is left blank here.",
  "AI 51 and AI 52 are both printed with \"(kvarh-)\"; the notes column marks them import (Q1+Q2) and export (Q3+Q4).",
  "The object list does not say which BACnet network the meter uses (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP); check Setra's SPM data sheet for the model."
 ],
